CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 4 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-read-implication
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
Covers the --no-read-implication opt-out, so the nested-mux form it restores
stays correct while the flattened form is the default. The companion test
read_implication_safe covers the default path, and between them both encodings
are exercised.

x = 2 is reachable only if a value travels from one thread to the other and
back, so the violation needs reads taking their values from writes in different
rounds in both directions. An implication form that lost a round, or pointed a
round at the wrong write, would make the assumptions unsatisfiable here and
report SUCCESSFUL having proved nothing.

Note a failing verdict cannot detect a constraint that is merely missing --
dropping constraints only adds behaviours, so the violation stays reachable.
That is what read_implication_safe is for.
